12
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:36,805
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

13
00:01:48,191 --> 00:01:49,276
[exhales softly]

14
00:01:52,029 --> 00:01:53,821
Where is Isoo right now?

15
00:01:53,822 --> 00:01:55,282
[♪ music increases in tempo]

16
00:01:57,284 --> 00:01:58,534
FINAL EPISODE

17
00:01:58,535 --> 00:02:00,161
Did he go to my exhibition hall?

18
00:02:00,162 --> 00:02:01,413
[♪ music swells]

19
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:05,499
[♪ music slows]

20
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,418
[♪ music increases in tempo]

21
00:02:07,419 --> 00:02:09,254
- [grunts, exclaims]
- [grunts]

22
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:11,840
- [Isoo grunts]
- [heavy thud]

23
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:15,677
[panting]

24
00:02:16,178 --> 00:02:17,220
[groans]

25
00:02:18,889 --> 00:02:20,556
- [blunt thud]
- [high-pitched ringing]

26
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:21,600
[thuds]

27
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:24,770
[high-pitched ringing fades]

28
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:28,565
[distorted thud]

29
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:33,945
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

30
00:02:43,872 --> 00:02:45,207
[line ringing]

31
00:02:50,087 --> 00:02:52,089
- [fire roaring]
- [cell phone vibrating]

32
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:06,561
[tires screech]

33
00:03:09,356 --> 00:03:10,815
How did it go?

34
00:03:10,816 --> 00:03:12,818
- There's a fire inside.
- What?

35
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:19,199
Isoo! Jin Isoo!

36
00:03:20,659 --> 00:03:21,910
Jin Isoo!

37
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:24,662
[♪ music increases in tempo]

38
00:03:24,663 --> 00:03:26,081
[grunts]

39
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:27,666
[all exclaim]

40
00:03:29,751 --> 00:03:30,752
Jin Isoo!

41
00:03:32,254 --> 00:03:33,672
Jin Isoo!

42
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:35,340
Isoo!

43
00:03:36,091 --> 00:03:37,884
Isoo! Jin Isoo!

44
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:39,469
Jin Isoo!

45
00:03:40,011 --> 00:03:41,930
Jin Isoo!

46
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:44,683
Get him on my back! [grunts]

47
00:03:45,434 --> 00:03:47,309
Jin Isoo! Get on my back!

48
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:48,895
[Changun grunting]

49
00:03:50,272 --> 00:03:51,689
Call an ambulance!

50
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:52,898
[♪ music resumes tempo]

51
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:53,900
[Changun grunts]

52
00:03:54,985 --> 00:03:56,153
[panting] Jin Isoo.

53
00:03:56,778 --> 00:03:57,987
Can you hear me?

54
00:03:57,988 --> 00:03:59,321
[sirens approaching]

55
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:01,490
The ambulance is on its way.
Hang in there.

56
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:02,659
[sirens blaring]

57
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:05,787
[tires screech]

58
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:10,207
[Changun] Here. He's here.

59
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:11,459
Over here!

60
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:13,503
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

61
00:04:18,175 --> 00:04:20,050
Detective Jin found all the evidence.

62
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:21,094
Evidence?

63
00:04:22,053 --> 00:04:23,054
What evidence?

64
00:04:25,891 --> 00:04:28,769
The victims' belongings and photos.

65
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:31,020
You have them all on display.

66
00:04:31,021 --> 00:04:32,022
Ah.

67
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:34,107
Really?

68
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:37,694
I wonder what he thought of it.

69
00:04:43,158 --> 00:04:44,825
[cell phone vibrating]

70
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:46,285
[♪ music fades]

71
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:48,163
CHIEF PARK CHANGUN

72
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:53,502
- You should get that.
- [cell phone continues vibrating]

73
00:04:54,169 --> 00:04:55,504
It seems urgent.

74
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:00,174
[panting] Detective Joo!

75
00:05:00,175 --> 00:05:02,010
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

76
00:05:07,766 --> 00:05:08,767
[door slams]

77
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:11,561
[breathes deeply]

78
00:05:12,771 --> 00:05:14,523
There's a basement inside my studio.

79
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:17,901
Tell your boyfriend to burn it down.

80
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:20,069
I might have a visitor.

81
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:21,488
[♪ music increases in tempo]

82
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:26,284
[♪ music swells, fades]

83
00:05:27,202 --> 00:05:28,453
[Hyera panting] Chief.

84
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:30,246
What about Isoo?

85
00:05:30,247 --> 00:05:31,413
Ah, well...

86
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:33,707
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

87
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:34,918
He's in surgery right now.

88
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:36,585
He has a brain hemorrhage.

89
00:05:36,586 --> 00:05:37,712
[sighs heavily]

90
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:41,591
[Hyera sighs softly]

91
00:05:43,343 --> 00:05:44,344
What do we do?

92
00:05:44,928 --> 00:05:46,262
Don't worry too much.

93
00:05:46,263 --> 00:05:48,013
They said they can stop the bleeding.

94
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:50,725
Detective Jin is going to be okay.

95
00:05:51,393 --> 00:05:52,977
What exactly happened?

96
00:05:52,978 --> 00:05:55,897
When we got there, Isoo was unconscious,

97
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:57,857
and the basement was on fire.

98
00:05:57,858 --> 00:06:00,901
- [exhales softly]
- You mean someone set the place on fire?

99
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:02,403
Yes.

100
00:06:02,404 --> 00:06:04,447
That person must have attacked Isoo.

101
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:08,243
We're searching through
all the nearby security footage...

102
00:06:09,995 --> 00:06:11,454
but the basement was destroyed.

103
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:13,456
We won't find any evidence.

104
00:06:14,124 --> 00:06:15,166
[sighs softly]

105
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:18,420
- [cell phone vibrating]
- [sighs heavily]

106
00:06:20,714 --> 00:06:21,798
Yes, how did it go?

107
00:06:23,008 --> 00:06:24,593
Then widen the search area.

108
00:06:25,594 --> 00:06:28,513
[angrily] Get a list of all the vehicles
spotted near the studio!

109
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,265
[Kyungjin sighs softly]

110
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:34,269
Yu Seongwon, that son of a bitch.

111
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:38,356
[voice shaking] I should've gone with him.

112
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:41,151
[sighs regretfully]

113
00:06:43,403 --> 00:06:45,572
- [Hyera sighs]
- [sighs heavily]

114
00:06:48,909 --> 00:06:51,411
The police chief said you are free to go.

115
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:56,291
SURGERY STATUS
JIN ISOO, 32Y/O MALE, IN SURGERY

116
00:06:59,419 --> 00:07:00,503
[♪ music fades]

117
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:04,882
Bro!

118
00:07:04,883 --> 00:07:07,260
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

119
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:09,011
How did it go?

120
00:07:09,012 --> 00:07:10,638
The surgery went well.

121
00:07:10,639 --> 00:07:14,558
But on top of the trauma to his brain,
he suffered carbon monoxide poisoning,

122
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:17,979
so it's difficult to say
when he will regain consciousness.

123
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:21,524
Right, we'll move him to his room.

124
00:07:42,754 --> 00:07:44,589
We'll look into the suspect's vehicle.

125
00:07:45,757 --> 00:07:46,841
Mmm.

126
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:05,902
Jin Isoo.

127
00:08:09,197 --> 00:08:10,281
You'll wake up, right?

128
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:17,914
I know you won't let this break you.

129
00:08:25,046 --> 00:08:26,047
I'll be waiting.

130
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,174
Sleep for a bit, then come back.

131
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:30,385
[♪ music swells]

132
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:32,469
[♪ music fades]

133
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:33,888
[cell phone vibrating]

134
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:42,229
Jin Isoo is still alive.

135
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:44,149
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

136
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:46,067
[line disconnects]

137
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:51,114
[monitor beeping steadily]

138
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:54,200
[♪ somber, melancholy music playing]

139
00:08:57,579 --> 00:08:58,663
Chairman Choi.

140
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:05,128
[breath trembles]

141
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:12,343
Detective Joo Hyera.

142
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:14,679
I'm sorry.

143
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:16,473
Please leave.

144
00:09:19,184 --> 00:09:21,019
I will stay here.

145
00:09:41,081 --> 00:09:42,123
[door closes]

146
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:02,476
[♪ music fades]

147
00:10:02,477 --> 00:10:06,314
NUMBER 1 SAFETY!! NUMBER 1 PUBLIC ORDER!!
GANGHA POLICE STATION

148
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:09,025
[sighs softly]

149
00:10:11,194 --> 00:10:12,319
[scoffs softly]

150
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:14,280
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

151
00:10:20,203 --> 00:10:21,913
[♪ music increases in tempo]

152
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:32,882
[exhales softly]

153
00:11:14,257 --> 00:11:15,925
Should I just disappear?

154
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:18,553
[scoffs softly]

155
00:11:19,596 --> 00:11:22,265
Should I make one final piece?

156
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:30,856
[♪ music fades]

157
00:11:30,857 --> 00:11:32,483
[monitor beeping steadily]

158
00:11:33,359 --> 00:11:35,320
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

159
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:53,254
[grunts softly]

160
00:12:01,346 --> 00:12:02,554
Is he awake?

161
00:12:02,555 --> 00:12:03,598
[sighs heavily]

162
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:09,395
No.

163
00:12:12,190 --> 00:12:13,191
Go on in.

164
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:15,818
I'll go talk to his doctor.

165
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:21,824
GANGHA JUNGANG HOSPITAL
VIP WING

166
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:30,750
[monitor beeping steadily]

167
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:37,799
[cell phone vibrating]

168
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:45,764
Hello?

169
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:47,432
[Kyungjin] <i>Is Isoo awake?</i>

170
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:48,810
He's still the same.

171
00:12:51,062 --> 00:12:52,437
Did you find anything?

172
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:54,606
We found a vehicle
that could be the suspect's,

173
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:55,858
but the plate is fake.

174
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:58,069
We'll keep looking.

175
00:13:05,952 --> 00:13:07,077
[♪ music fades]

176
00:13:07,078 --> 00:13:08,288
[Kyungjin sighs softly]

177
00:13:09,372 --> 00:13:10,665
[Junyoung exhales softly]

178
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,125
[pats back]

179
00:13:13,126 --> 00:13:15,502
Get it together.
We need to catch that bastard.

180
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:17,380
[sighs deeply] Okay.

181
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:20,674
[sighs heavily]
I don't know about Yu Seongwon,

182
00:13:20,675 --> 00:13:22,885
but if Jeong Taeseon ordered
someone to do it,

183
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:25,304
it's probably him.

184
00:13:25,305 --> 00:13:27,055
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

185
00:13:27,056 --> 00:13:29,641
But he went off the grid
after killing Cho Pilgu.

186
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:30,976
We don't even know his name.

187
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:32,020
[sighs thoughtfully]

188
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:35,480
Is there any way to track the car
after it left the studio?

189
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:37,775
I checked all the traffic cameras,
but it disappeared.

190
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:41,946
Did the suspect ditch the car somewhere?

191
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:45,825
Let's search the area again
from where it disappeared.

192
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:51,246
Mmm, the car disappeared around here.

193
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:52,915
- Let's go.
- [cell phone vibrating]

194
00:13:54,459 --> 00:13:55,835
INCOMING CALL
NO CALLER ID

195
00:14:02,884 --> 00:14:04,719
Yes, this is Park Junyoung.

196
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:06,554
[unknown caller] <i>Ah.</i>

197
00:14:07,305 --> 00:14:09,932
We are Detective Jin Isoo's... [mouthing]

198
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:13,560
His secret agents.

199
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:14,853
What?

200
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:17,899
<i>We saw on the news
that Detective Jin was in an accident.</i>

201
00:14:18,733 --> 00:14:19,734
So?

202
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:23,946
He asked us to find someone for him.

203
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,323
[whispering] A guy who killed a suspect.

204
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:27,449
Did you find him?

205
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:28,992
[secret agent] <i>We found him.</i>

206
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:30,202
How?

207
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:31,286
Ah.

208
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:32,496
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

209
00:14:32,497 --> 00:14:34,040
That will remain a secret.

210
00:14:34,665 --> 00:14:36,249
His name is Han Jonghyeon.

211
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:37,919
Date of birth is November 19, 1983.

212
00:14:40,671 --> 00:14:43,049
IDENTITY SEARCH

213
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:49,639
NAME HAN JONGHYEON

214
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:53,016
[secret agent] <i>His recent location
is Wonmok-dong.</i>

215
00:14:53,017 --> 00:14:55,977
It seems he's at a hotel
called East Hill Hotel.

216
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:56,979
Thank you.

217
00:14:57,772 --> 00:14:58,898
- Let's go.
- Okay.

218
00:15:01,943 --> 00:15:02,985
[♪ music fades]

219
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:06,781
[cell phone vibrating]

220
00:15:10,785 --> 00:15:11,868
Hello?

221
00:15:11,869 --> 00:15:13,578
[Taeseon] No matter how I look at it...

222
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:14,913
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

223
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:16,791
...to cover all this up,

224
00:15:19,252 --> 00:15:21,629
I think Seongwon
will have to commit suicide.

225
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:26,424
<i>A mentally unstable artist</i>

226
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:28,427
takes his life
after his studio burns down.

227
00:15:30,012 --> 00:15:31,805
The murder cases are closed unsolved.

228
00:15:31,806 --> 00:15:34,225
[♪ ominous chord swells, fades]

229
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:38,813
And I'll become a poor mother

230
00:15:40,398 --> 00:15:42,650
who lost her child.

231
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:44,318
Yes, understood.

232
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:46,904
<i>Do you still have what I gave you?</i>

233
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:50,031
He's not easy to deal with.

234
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:51,533
[♪ music increases in tempo]

235
00:15:51,534 --> 00:15:53,536
There's no telling what he'll do.
Be careful.

236
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:55,830
<i>When it's done,</i>

237
00:15:56,706 --> 00:15:58,081
<i>leave the country.</i>

238
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,959
I'll come find you.

239
00:16:01,335 --> 00:16:02,712
<i>I'm always grateful to you.</i>

240
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:06,382
You know you're the only one
I can trust, right?

241
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:10,177
Yes. Please don't worry.

242
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:11,554
[♪ music swells]

243
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:21,480
[♪ music fades]

244
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:26,943
It's this place.

245
00:16:26,944 --> 00:16:28,403
EAST HILL HOTEL

246
00:16:28,404 --> 00:16:30,031
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

247
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:33,075
That's Han Jonghyeon.

248
00:16:36,162 --> 00:16:37,245
You're right.

249
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:38,456
[♪ music increases in tempo]

250
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:51,510
[♪ music swells]

251
00:16:58,517 --> 00:16:59,602
[♪ music fades]

252
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:02,772
- [cell phone vibrating]
- [exhales sharply]

253
00:17:04,565 --> 00:17:06,567
JEONG TAESEON

254
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:11,948
[sighs softly]

255
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:17,577
[Taeseon] <i>I sent you a car.
Come to the villa.</i>

256
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:19,413
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

257
00:17:27,797 --> 00:17:28,798
Should we get him now?

258
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:30,299
No.

259
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:32,384
Let's wait and see.

260
00:17:32,385 --> 00:17:33,427
[exhales softly]

261
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:43,062
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

262
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:48,859
- [sighs softly]
- Please get in.

263
00:17:50,403 --> 00:17:52,154
The chairwoman sent me to escort you.

264
00:17:55,950 --> 00:17:57,076
[inhales sharply]

265
00:18:29,609 --> 00:18:30,860
[cell phone vibrating]

266
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:36,990
Detective Joo, we found the suspect
who killed Cho Pilgu.

267
00:18:36,991 --> 00:18:39,868
Han Jonghyeon used to be
Jeong Taeseon's chief secretary.

268
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:41,870
<i>He's on the move with Yu Seongwon.</i>

269
00:18:41,871 --> 00:18:42,954
We're following them.

270
00:18:42,955 --> 00:18:45,248
Where are you? I'll be right there.

271
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:47,293
Near Haseong. We'll keep you updated.

272
00:18:48,919 --> 00:18:50,254
[♪ music swells]

273
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:57,802
[♪ music fades]

274
00:18:57,803 --> 00:18:59,054
[Seongwon sighs softly]

275
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:01,431
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

276
00:19:01,432 --> 00:19:02,516
Where are we going?

277
00:19:03,184 --> 00:19:04,977
This isn't the way to the villa.

278
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:17,865
[sighs deeply]

279
00:19:23,537 --> 00:19:25,373
Did my mom tell you to kill me?

280
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:33,505
Did she tell you
to lock me up in a psych ward again?

281
00:19:33,506 --> 00:19:35,383
[breathes deeply]

282
00:19:40,137 --> 00:19:42,348
That's what you get for pushing your luck.

283
00:19:44,058 --> 00:19:45,976
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

284
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,365
[Seongwon exhales heavily]

285
00:20:01,784 --> 00:20:03,369
[♪ music increases in tempo]

286
00:20:04,537 --> 00:20:05,579
[scoffing softly]

287
00:20:07,957 --> 00:20:10,084
[♪ music turns ominous]

288
00:20:13,379 --> 00:20:15,005
- [distant gunshot]
- What was that?

289
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:17,006
[engine revving]

290
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:18,134
[♪ music swells]

291
00:20:19,719 --> 00:20:22,053
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

292
00:20:22,054 --> 00:20:23,347
[tires screech]

293
00:20:28,561 --> 00:20:29,936
[♪ music increases in tempo]

294
00:20:29,937 --> 00:20:31,689
- [tires screeching]
- [engine revving]

295
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:34,566
[tires screeching]

296
00:20:34,567 --> 00:20:36,110
[engine accelerating]

297
00:20:38,279 --> 00:20:39,780
- [explosive crash]
- [glass shattering]

298
00:20:42,283 --> 00:20:44,118
- [violent crunching]
- [debris rattling]

299
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:50,332
[chuckles]

300
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,543
- [engine whirring in reverse]
- [tires screeching]

301
00:20:53,544 --> 00:20:55,045
- [engine revving]
- [tires screeching]

302
00:20:55,504 --> 00:20:57,339
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

303
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:05,723
[motorcycle approaching]

304
00:21:08,434 --> 00:21:10,143
[♪ music increases in tempo]

305
00:21:10,144 --> 00:21:11,479
[engine idles, shuts off]

306
00:21:18,903 --> 00:21:20,070
[♪ music resumes tempo]

307
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:22,072
[♪ music increases in tempo]

308
00:21:39,215 --> 00:21:40,382
[leaves rustling]

309
00:21:41,342 --> 00:21:42,384
[grunts]

310
00:21:43,344 --> 00:21:44,345
Detective Park.

311
00:21:45,930 --> 00:21:47,223
Detective Choi!

312
00:21:48,057 --> 00:21:49,975
Detective Park, wake up.
[breathing frantically]

313
00:21:51,352 --> 00:21:52,520
[♪ music fades]

314
00:21:52,895 --> 00:21:54,979
EMERGENCY WARD

315
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,232
[monitors beeping steadily]

316
00:21:58,526 --> 00:21:59,527
[hisses in pain]

317
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:06,200
- [sighs softly]
- [cell phone vibrating]

318
00:22:07,785 --> 00:22:09,035
Hello?

319
00:22:09,036 --> 00:22:11,162
[Byungsik] Yu Seongwon ditched the car
and disappeared.

320
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:12,623
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

321
00:22:13,374 --> 00:22:15,125
There aren't any cameras here.

322
00:22:15,835 --> 00:22:17,336
We'll widen the search area.

323
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:20,089
[sighs wearily]

324
00:22:23,592 --> 00:22:24,593
[panting] Junyoung.

325
00:22:26,595 --> 00:22:27,596
Jiwon.

326
00:22:28,389 --> 00:22:30,306
How did this happen?

327
00:22:30,307 --> 00:22:31,391
You're badly hurt.

328
00:22:31,392 --> 00:22:34,728
No, I just hurt my neck a little.

329
00:22:35,688 --> 00:22:36,730
[shuddering exhale]

330
00:22:37,648 --> 00:22:38,732
I'm sorry.

331
00:22:40,359 --> 00:22:41,402
It's fine.

332
00:22:42,736 --> 00:22:43,946
I'm just glad you're okay.

333
00:22:44,613 --> 00:22:45,781
[inhales softly]

334
00:22:49,952 --> 00:22:51,120
[Hyera sighs softly]

335
00:22:52,663 --> 00:22:54,123
[Hyera] We're out of options. [sighs]

336
00:22:57,084 --> 00:22:58,586
I'll finish this.

337
00:23:05,342 --> 00:23:06,843
Please look after Isoo.

338
00:23:06,844 --> 00:23:08,470
[♪ music increases in tempo]

339
00:23:15,269 --> 00:23:16,352
[♪ music fades]

340
00:23:16,353 --> 00:23:18,104
JONGHYEON

341
00:23:18,105 --> 00:23:19,523
[line ringing]

342
00:23:23,319 --> 00:23:25,445
[automated voice] <i>The number
you have dialed is unavailable...</i>

343
00:23:25,446 --> 00:23:26,988
You can't go in there.

344
00:23:26,989 --> 00:23:29,116
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

345
00:23:33,871 --> 00:23:36,873
Han Jonghyeon was murdered.

346
00:23:36,874 --> 00:23:37,917
[door closes]

347
00:23:45,090 --> 00:23:47,009
Did you order him to kill Yu Seongwon?

348
00:23:49,428 --> 00:23:51,596
What do you mean?
This looks like an accident.

349
00:23:51,597 --> 00:23:54,432
My team was following Han Jonghyeon.

350
00:23:54,433 --> 00:23:57,603
Yu Seongwon killed him and disappeared.

351
00:23:59,355 --> 00:24:00,397
So what?

352
00:24:01,690 --> 00:24:02,942
Yu Seongwon will now

353
00:24:04,026 --> 00:24:05,736
come to kill you.

354
00:24:06,737 --> 00:24:07,821
[scoffs]

355
00:24:08,656 --> 00:24:11,533
- Hmm.
- All the evidence is gone,

356
00:24:13,035 --> 00:24:15,371
and he may have considered
leaving like this,

357
00:24:16,163 --> 00:24:18,499
but now that his own mother
tried to kill him,

358
00:24:19,083 --> 00:24:20,167
he won't hold back.

359
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:25,505
He's been obsessed with dead bodies
and murder since he was a child.

360
00:24:25,506 --> 00:24:26,507
You knew, didn't you?

361
00:24:28,175 --> 00:24:30,803
But all you did was
try to hide it and cover it up.

362
00:24:31,845 --> 00:24:33,222
You'll pay the price for that.

363
00:24:34,765 --> 00:24:35,891
If you cooperate with us

364
00:24:37,935 --> 00:24:39,895
and confess to everything that's happened,

365
00:24:40,688 --> 00:24:41,772
we'll protect you.

366
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:44,441
You will

367
00:24:45,317 --> 00:24:46,818
protect me?

368
00:24:46,819 --> 00:24:47,944
Yes.

369
00:24:47,945 --> 00:24:49,737
If it means we can catch Yu Seongwon.

370
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:51,198
[scoffs] I don't need it.

371
00:24:52,032 --> 00:24:53,908
I know my son best.

372
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:54,910
That boy...

373
00:24:56,912 --> 00:24:58,205
can't go against me.

374
00:24:59,498 --> 00:25:01,542
Without me, his life is over, too.

375
00:25:02,626 --> 00:25:04,420
If we don't catch Yu Seongwon now,

376
00:25:05,838 --> 00:25:08,716
you'll have to spend
the rest of your life living in fear.

377
00:25:10,259 --> 00:25:12,094
Never knowing when your son...

378
00:25:13,303 --> 00:25:15,806
might sneak in and kill you.

379
00:25:19,184 --> 00:25:20,436
Are you okay with that?

380
00:25:32,698 --> 00:25:35,868
Then the next time I see you,
I'll be looking at your dead body.

381
00:25:38,412 --> 00:25:39,955
[footsteps receding]

382
00:25:44,668 --> 00:25:46,754
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

383
00:25:58,766 --> 00:26:00,184
[♪ music increases in tempo]

384
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:39,723
[♪ music fades]

385
00:26:41,558 --> 00:26:43,101
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

386
00:26:43,102 --> 00:26:44,103
Mom.

387
00:26:46,021 --> 00:26:47,272
What are you doing here?

388
00:26:48,857 --> 00:26:50,359
You don't come to my exhibitions.

389
00:26:51,985 --> 00:26:53,153
What?

390
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:55,489
Are you worried there's evidence here?

391
00:26:59,952 --> 00:27:00,994
[sighs]

392
00:27:01,453 --> 00:27:04,206
Now you're trying
to get rid of my work, too?

393
00:27:04,832 --> 00:27:05,916
[Seongwon] Huh?

394
00:27:07,126 --> 00:27:08,168
[♪ music swells]

395
00:27:11,380 --> 00:27:12,464
[♪ music fades]

396
00:27:15,884 --> 00:27:16,885
Joo Hyera?

397
00:27:21,390 --> 00:27:22,557
[sighs softly]

398
00:27:22,558 --> 00:27:24,350
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

399
00:27:24,351 --> 00:27:27,396
You posed as the victims
to create an alibi, didn't you?

400
00:27:28,897 --> 00:27:30,357
I tried it myself.

401
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:33,610
How does it feel
to be on the receiving end?

402
00:27:34,403 --> 00:27:35,445
[sighs softly]

403
00:27:36,905 --> 00:27:40,158
Then the next time I see you,
I'll be looking at your dead body.

404
00:27:40,742 --> 00:27:42,035
[footsteps receding]

405
00:27:44,663 --> 00:27:45,746
[Taeseon] Wait.

406
00:27:45,747 --> 00:27:47,708
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

407
00:27:50,669 --> 00:27:52,004
How will you catch him?

408
00:27:54,548 --> 00:27:56,174
I'll pretend to be you.

409
00:27:57,551 --> 00:27:58,552
What?

410
00:27:59,428 --> 00:28:01,471
Are you disappointed I'm not your mom?

411
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:04,850
No, it's fine.

412
00:28:05,642 --> 00:28:09,186
[exhales softly] I've always wanted
to use you as a model, too.

413
00:28:09,187 --> 00:28:11,022
The detective who was after me

414
00:28:11,023 --> 00:28:13,984
failed to catch me
and became my art in the end.

415
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:15,402
[chuckles]

416
00:28:18,697 --> 00:28:19,698
Joo Hyera.

417
00:28:22,993 --> 00:28:24,744
How do you want to die?

418
00:28:24,745 --> 00:28:25,995
[♪ music turns ominous]

419
00:28:25,996 --> 00:28:27,039
[scoffs]

420
00:28:28,206 --> 00:28:29,583
How do you want to die?

421
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:32,169
Today's that day.

422
00:28:33,295 --> 00:28:35,296
I was obsessed with you.

423
00:28:35,297 --> 00:28:36,840
I wanted to stop you.

424
00:28:38,008 --> 00:28:39,384
And I wanted to catch you.

425
00:28:40,344 --> 00:28:42,387
But now I'm out of options.

426
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:46,099
I'll have to kill you.

427
00:28:46,516 --> 00:28:47,643
[scoffs]

428
00:28:48,185 --> 00:28:49,937
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

429
00:28:50,354 --> 00:28:51,772
[grunts, groans]

430
00:28:52,606 --> 00:28:53,690
[groans]

431
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:55,776
[Seongwon grunting]

432
00:28:57,069 --> 00:28:58,445
- [exhales sharply]
- [grunts]

433
00:28:59,237 --> 00:29:00,280
[groaning]

434
00:29:01,323 --> 00:29:02,616
[dull thud]

435
00:29:03,408 --> 00:29:04,492
Do you get it now?

436
00:29:04,493 --> 00:29:05,701
[groaning]

437
00:29:05,702 --> 00:29:07,703
This is the death you love so much.

438
00:29:07,704 --> 00:29:09,455
[laughing maniacally]

439
00:29:09,456 --> 00:29:10,957
[breathing heavily]

440
00:29:10,958 --> 00:29:13,250
You... [exhales heavily]

441
00:29:13,251 --> 00:29:14,461
...will become a masterpiece.

442
00:29:15,837 --> 00:29:16,964
- [gunshot]
- [squelch]

443
00:29:20,008 --> 00:29:21,217
[distorted thud]

444
00:29:21,218 --> 00:29:23,095
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

445
00:29:26,515 --> 00:29:27,683
[sighs in relief]

446
00:29:31,061 --> 00:29:32,229
[chuckles]

447
00:29:37,317 --> 00:29:38,443
[grunts softly]

448
00:29:46,827 --> 00:29:48,829
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

449
00:29:54,376 --> 00:29:55,377
[exhales sharply]

450
00:30:07,431 --> 00:30:08,473
[exhales sharply]

451
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:17,441
[♪ music increases in tempo]

452
00:30:17,983 --> 00:30:19,026
[exhales sharply]

453
00:30:25,866 --> 00:30:27,366
[Isoo] Yu Seongwon!

454
00:30:27,367 --> 00:30:29,285
[♪ music resumes tempo]

455
00:30:29,286 --> 00:30:30,369
Isoo!

456
00:30:30,370 --> 00:30:32,455
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

457
00:30:32,456 --> 00:30:33,582
I'm glad you're here.

458
00:30:34,458 --> 00:30:36,209
You need to witness this piece.

459
00:30:38,253 --> 00:30:39,421
You crazy bastard.

460
00:30:42,174 --> 00:30:43,675
It's not finished yet.

461
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:47,887
Just watch how I turn this woman
into a work of art.

462
00:30:47,888 --> 00:30:50,557
It's the final piece you'll see
before you die.

463
00:30:51,725 --> 00:30:52,726
A work of art?

464
00:30:55,228 --> 00:30:56,396
[♪ music swells]

465
00:31:01,109 --> 00:31:02,359
[shattering]

466
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:04,112
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

467
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:06,073
Is this a work of art?

468
00:31:10,786 --> 00:31:12,204
[shattering, scattering]

469
00:31:13,205 --> 00:31:14,414
[panting]

470
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:17,167
This is a work of art?

471
00:31:19,711 --> 00:31:21,171
This is just garbage.

472
00:31:24,716 --> 00:31:27,010
Garbage created by a psychotic killer.

473
00:31:28,887 --> 00:31:30,514
You think you're an artist?

474
00:31:31,598 --> 00:31:33,642
You just want to kill people.

475
00:31:34,684 --> 00:31:37,354
Because you have
this sick obsession with dead bodies.

476
00:31:39,564 --> 00:31:41,941
You dress it up as art

477
00:31:41,942 --> 00:31:44,319
and proudly show it off
for people to see...

478
00:31:47,572 --> 00:31:49,157
but you're just insane.

479
00:31:50,033 --> 00:31:51,284
[sighs heavily]

480
00:31:51,993 --> 00:31:53,495
Do you still not get it?

481
00:31:54,079 --> 00:31:56,623
This is art on a whole other level!

482
00:31:57,541 --> 00:31:58,833
The people I killed

483
00:31:58,834 --> 00:32:01,502
were living meaningless lives.

484
00:32:01,503 --> 00:32:04,798
But I turned them
into something eternally beautiful!

485
00:32:07,551 --> 00:32:08,634
Jo Nayeong.

486
00:32:08,635 --> 00:32:10,803
She couldn't get hired
as a flight attendant,

487
00:32:10,804 --> 00:32:13,389
so she went from
one part-time job to another.

488
00:32:13,390 --> 00:32:16,016
She lived a miserable life
in a basement studio,

489
00:32:16,017 --> 00:32:18,436
but I turned her into something beautiful!

490
00:32:19,688 --> 00:32:21,773
- [Nayeong whimpering softly]
- [Seongwon grunting]

491
00:32:24,901 --> 00:32:27,154
- [whimpering]
- [grunting]

492
00:32:31,408 --> 00:32:32,741
ECSTASY
A BREATHLESS FALL

493
00:32:32,742 --> 00:32:35,995
No one so much as gave her a second look
when she was alive.

494
00:32:35,996 --> 00:32:39,457
But now everyone looks at her
and calls her a beautiful work of art.

495
00:32:41,126 --> 00:32:42,794
Choi Yeongmin.

496
00:32:46,840 --> 00:32:48,508
He had a great body.

497
00:32:49,676 --> 00:32:51,178
So I used a knife.

498
00:32:53,180 --> 00:32:55,640
[♪ melancholy piano music playing]

499
00:32:56,391 --> 00:32:57,601
- [squelch]
- [blood splatters]

500
00:32:59,603 --> 00:33:00,853
[♪ ominous sting plays]

501
00:33:00,854 --> 00:33:02,022
[chuckles softly]

502
00:33:04,024 --> 00:33:05,524
[Seongwon] <i>The blood in the air</i>

503
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:07,318
looked like stars.

504
00:33:07,319 --> 00:33:09,029
CLIMAX
LIGHT SCATTERED ACROSS THE UNIVERSE

505
00:33:12,032 --> 00:33:13,491
And Jeong Minjae.

506
00:33:15,076 --> 00:33:16,952
He blossomed like a flower.

507
00:33:16,953 --> 00:33:18,205
[wet dripping]

508
00:33:34,304 --> 00:33:35,555
[laughs maliciously]

509
00:33:40,560 --> 00:33:42,938
Do you know why people love my work?

510
00:33:44,064 --> 00:33:47,942
They can feel that death is present here
without needing to be told.

511
00:33:47,943 --> 00:33:49,986
Everyone has that urge.

512
00:33:50,528 --> 00:33:51,738
"I want to know death."

513
00:33:52,489 --> 00:33:54,156
"I want to see death."

514
00:33:54,157 --> 00:33:56,033
In the past, they held public executions.

515
00:33:56,034 --> 00:33:59,161
The people watching
would've felt a sense of catharsis.

516
00:33:59,162 --> 00:34:01,997
The exhilaration of being alive
in the face of death.

517
00:34:01,998 --> 00:34:04,041
The desire for true life!

518
00:34:04,042 --> 00:34:05,209
[yelling] That!

519
00:34:05,210 --> 00:34:07,879
That is what I showed them!

520
00:34:08,380 --> 00:34:09,506
[♪ music swells]

521
00:34:12,968 --> 00:34:14,051
[♪ music fades]

522
00:34:14,052 --> 00:34:15,512
I think this is enough.

523
00:34:16,137 --> 00:34:17,388
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

524
00:34:17,389 --> 00:34:18,890
[Hyera] Thanks for the confession.

525
00:34:21,977 --> 00:34:24,604
[♪ dramatic sting plays]

526
00:34:26,314 --> 00:34:27,439
[♪ music fades]

527
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:28,524
FOUR HOURS EARLIER

528
00:34:28,525 --> 00:34:30,360
We're out of options. [sighs]

529
00:34:30,735 --> 00:34:32,903
- I'll finish this.
- [monitor beeping steadily]

530
00:34:32,904 --> 00:34:34,864
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

531
00:34:38,660 --> 00:34:39,869
Please look after Isoo.

532
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:43,164
Mmm.

533
00:34:49,879 --> 00:34:51,506
[Isoo, muffled]
What are you planning to do?

534
00:34:52,549 --> 00:34:53,550
[Mr. Choi] Isoo!

535
00:34:57,846 --> 00:34:59,347
- [Hyera] Are you okay?
- [groans softly]

536
00:35:00,223 --> 00:35:01,266
[exhales heavily]

537
00:35:03,476 --> 00:35:06,021
I slept like a log
and now I'm completely refreshed.

538
00:35:06,605 --> 00:35:07,647
[sighs in relief]

539
00:35:08,231 --> 00:35:09,232
So?

540
00:35:10,191 --> 00:35:11,942
How are you going to finish this?

541
00:35:11,943 --> 00:35:13,028
Ah... [sighs]

542
00:35:14,237 --> 00:35:17,115
I'll have to pressure
Jeong Taeseon into confessing.

543
00:35:20,076 --> 00:35:22,078
That won't work on her.

544
00:35:28,335 --> 00:35:29,835
Let's set something up.

545
00:35:29,836 --> 00:35:31,796
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

546
00:35:33,965 --> 00:35:35,216
He has a gun?

547
00:35:35,925 --> 00:35:37,134
Yes.

548
00:35:37,135 --> 00:35:39,012
Han Jonghyeon had a gun,

549
00:35:39,596 --> 00:35:40,805
and Yu Seongwon took it.

550
00:35:41,348 --> 00:35:42,766
[panting softly]

551
00:35:46,811 --> 00:35:48,605
Then he'll get even more reckless.

552
00:35:50,523 --> 00:35:51,524
Actually,

553
00:35:52,942 --> 00:35:54,486
that could work to our advantage.

554
00:35:55,278 --> 00:35:56,279
What?

555
00:35:57,405 --> 00:35:59,823
I'll be the bait and lure Yu Seongwon out.

556
00:35:59,824 --> 00:36:00,825
No.

557
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:03,744
I'll be the bait.

558
00:36:03,745 --> 00:36:05,245
Just explain what the plan is.

559
00:36:05,246 --> 00:36:06,373
[♪ music swells]

560
00:36:08,625 --> 00:36:10,085
- [exhales heavily]
- [♪ music fades]

561
00:36:13,254 --> 00:36:14,546
[vest straps fastening]

562
00:36:14,547 --> 00:36:15,590
[sighs in exasperation]

563
00:36:16,633 --> 00:36:17,925
[Velcro ripping]

564
00:36:17,926 --> 00:36:20,094
I still think it's too dangerous.

565
00:36:20,095 --> 00:36:21,261
Will you be okay?

566
00:36:21,262 --> 00:36:22,347
[Velcro ripping]

567
00:36:22,806 --> 00:36:23,807
[sighs softly]

568
00:36:26,768 --> 00:36:28,560
- I'll make him shoot here.
- [sighs in exasperation]

569
00:36:28,561 --> 00:36:29,979
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

570
00:36:31,648 --> 00:36:32,941
[Velcro ripping]

571
00:36:34,317 --> 00:36:37,277
Isoo. You're still not fully recovered.

572
00:36:37,278 --> 00:36:39,071
I'm really excited right now.

573
00:36:39,072 --> 00:36:42,742
I feel great just thinking
about catching Yu Seongwon. Mmm!

574
00:36:43,952 --> 00:36:44,953
Mr. Choi.

575
00:36:45,578 --> 00:36:46,871
I need to ask you a favor.

576
00:36:47,789 --> 00:36:50,999
Please get the press together
so we can broadcast live.

577
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:54,336
UBS might try something,
so call all the foreign outlets, too.

578
00:36:54,337 --> 00:36:55,880
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

579
00:36:57,549 --> 00:36:58,675
All right.

580
00:36:59,926 --> 00:37:01,010
I'm off.

581
00:37:07,267 --> 00:37:08,435
[grunts, groans]

582
00:37:09,519 --> 00:37:10,603
[groans]

583
00:37:11,062 --> 00:37:12,272
- [exhales sharply]
- [grunts softly]

584
00:37:12,897 --> 00:37:14,273
[grunts]

585
00:37:14,274 --> 00:37:15,859
You... [breathing heavily]

586
00:37:17,193 --> 00:37:18,403
...will become a masterpiece.

587
00:37:19,988 --> 00:37:21,072
- [gunshot]
- [squelch]

588
00:37:22,073 --> 00:37:24,951
[Isoo] <i>Because you have
this sick obsession with dead bodies.</i>

589
00:37:25,577 --> 00:37:27,369
You dress it up as art

590
00:37:27,370 --> 00:37:30,081
and proudly show it off
for people to see...

591
00:37:31,374 --> 00:37:32,667
but you're just insane.

592
00:37:33,126 --> 00:37:35,669
[sighs heavily] Do you still not get it?

593
00:37:35,670 --> 00:37:38,298
This is art on a whole other level!

594
00:37:39,132 --> 00:37:40,215
The people I killed

595
00:37:40,216 --> 00:37:43,051
were living meaningless lives.

596
00:37:43,052 --> 00:37:46,514
But I turned them
into something eternally beautiful!

597
00:37:47,015 --> 00:37:48,098
Jo Nayeong.

598
00:37:48,099 --> 00:37:50,184
She couldn't get hired
as a flight attendant,

599
00:37:50,185 --> 00:37:53,061
<i>so she went from
one part-time job to another.</i>

600
00:37:53,062 --> 00:37:55,355
<i>She lived a miserable life
in a basement studio,</i>

601
00:37:55,356 --> 00:37:56,982
<i>but I turned her into something beautiful!</i>

602
00:37:56,983 --> 00:38:00,027
Everyone, this is a secret mission,
so please just watch quietly.

603
00:38:00,028 --> 00:38:01,528
- What's the secret mission?
- [reporters murmuring]

604
00:38:01,529 --> 00:38:02,905
[reporter 1] What's going on?

605
00:38:02,906 --> 00:38:05,991
<i>They can feel that death is present here
without needing to be told.</i>

606
00:38:05,992 --> 00:38:07,911
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

607
00:38:09,162 --> 00:38:10,370
[chuckles]

608
00:38:10,371 --> 00:38:11,623
- [♪ music swells]
- [gunshot]

609
00:38:11,998 --> 00:38:13,457
- [grunts]
- [heavy thud]

610
00:38:13,458 --> 00:38:15,292
[♪ theme music playing]

611
00:38:15,293 --> 00:38:16,628
[panting] Crazy bastard.

612
00:38:19,255 --> 00:38:20,256
Here.

613
00:38:27,180 --> 00:38:28,389
- Yu Seongwon.
- [handcuffs clicking]

614
00:38:29,015 --> 00:38:30,350
For the murders of Jo Nayeong...

615
00:38:31,810 --> 00:38:35,479
- [whimpers]
- [Hyera] ...Choi Yeongmin, Kim Heejun,

616
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:39,024
and Jeong Minjae, you are under arrest.

617
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:40,235
[breathing heavily]

618
00:38:43,655 --> 00:38:44,781
[murmuring]

619
00:38:54,290 --> 00:38:55,541
There they come.

620
00:38:55,542 --> 00:38:56,543
[reporter 2] He's here!

621
00:38:58,545 --> 00:39:01,046
[reporter 3] Did you confess
to the serial murders?

622
00:39:01,047 --> 00:39:02,965
[reporter 4] When did you
first start killing people?

623
00:39:02,966 --> 00:39:04,259
[clamoring]

624
00:39:06,553 --> 00:39:08,054
You're a pretty big name,

625
00:39:08,888 --> 00:39:11,182
so I called all the foreign press here.

626
00:39:11,975 --> 00:39:13,309
[clamoring continues]

627
00:39:22,861 --> 00:39:24,069
[♪ music fades]

628
00:39:24,070 --> 00:39:25,153
[newscaster 1] <i>This is breaking news.</i>

629
00:39:25,154 --> 00:39:29,283
<i>Sculptor Yu Seongwon's serial murder
confession was broadcast live tonight.</i>

630
00:39:29,284 --> 00:39:32,786
<i>In a shocking revelation, the victims
were the models for his artwork.</i>

631
00:39:32,787 --> 00:39:34,329
[newscaster 2, in English]
<i>This is ANN News.</i>

632
00:39:34,330 --> 00:39:38,333
<i>Seongwon Yu confessed he derived pleasure
from killing his victims.</i>

633
00:39:38,334 --> 00:39:40,294
<i>Prosecutors say he showed no remorse,</i>

634
00:39:40,295 --> 00:39:43,547
<i>even going so far as to belittle
the lives of those he killed.</i>

635
00:39:43,548 --> 00:39:46,425
[newscaster 3] <i>Meanwhile,
police have opened an investigation</i>

636
00:39:46,426 --> 00:39:49,553
<i>after reports suggested
there may have been similar disappearances</i>

637
00:39:49,554 --> 00:39:52,140
<i>during the time Yu was studying
in the United Kingdom.</i>

638
00:39:55,685 --> 00:39:58,187
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

639
00:40:09,198 --> 00:40:10,241
[door closes]

640
00:40:15,955 --> 00:40:17,081
Why aren't you going in?

641
00:40:18,750 --> 00:40:19,834
Ah.

642
00:40:20,335 --> 00:40:21,752
I handed in my resignation.

643
00:40:21,753 --> 00:40:22,754
Your resignation...

644
00:40:23,755 --> 00:40:24,838
has been rejected.

645
00:40:24,839 --> 00:40:26,549
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

646
00:40:31,012 --> 00:40:32,180
Now, go.

647
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:34,599
Take him down.

648
00:40:36,643 --> 00:40:37,644
Yes, Chief.

649
00:40:41,856 --> 00:40:42,857
[♪ music fades]

650
00:40:44,359 --> 00:40:45,610
[Isoo exhales contentedly]

651
00:40:46,986 --> 00:40:48,820
All right, since you've already confessed,

652
00:40:48,821 --> 00:40:50,698
let's have an honest conversation.

653
00:40:51,991 --> 00:40:52,992
Confessed?

654
00:40:54,369 --> 00:40:57,080
Was that a confession?

655
00:40:58,164 --> 00:41:00,040
What I said earlier

656
00:41:00,041 --> 00:41:03,585
was about the things I'd imagined
while working with those models.

657
00:41:03,586 --> 00:41:04,712
It's not real.

658
00:41:06,047 --> 00:41:07,632
Wait, you actually believed that?

659
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:11,469
Was my acting that convincing?

660
00:41:13,137 --> 00:41:15,390
Forensics is investigating
your studio right now.

661
00:41:16,474 --> 00:41:18,350
Let's see how you hold out
until we find the evidence.

662
00:41:18,351 --> 00:41:19,352
Evidence?

663
00:41:20,103 --> 00:41:21,145
Will you find any?

664
00:41:22,188 --> 00:41:24,231
Someone seems to have burned it down.

665
00:41:24,232 --> 00:41:25,942
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

666
00:41:39,414 --> 00:41:40,581
[objects clattering]

667
00:41:43,001 --> 00:41:44,544
[♪ music increases in tempo]

668
00:41:49,090 --> 00:41:51,299
[distant clanking]

669
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:52,969
[camera shutter clicking]

670
00:42:05,106 --> 00:42:06,190
[♪ music swells]

671
00:42:11,446 --> 00:42:12,488
[cell phone vibrates]

672
00:42:13,072 --> 00:42:15,657
Detective Park,
I noticed something strange.

673
00:42:15,658 --> 00:42:16,868
[♪ music fades]

674
00:42:20,329 --> 00:42:21,330
Hey.

675
00:42:22,540 --> 00:42:23,541
By any chance,

676
00:42:24,208 --> 00:42:25,460
are you waiting for you mom?

677
00:42:26,294 --> 00:42:28,170
She's in the next room.

678
00:42:28,171 --> 00:42:30,464
She's here to cooperate
with the investigation

679
00:42:30,465 --> 00:42:32,507
and reveal the entire truth.

680
00:42:32,508 --> 00:42:33,925
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

681
00:42:33,926 --> 00:42:35,678
It's time you stood on your own two feet.

682
00:42:36,512 --> 00:42:38,473
You can't depend on your mom forever.

683
00:42:42,018 --> 00:42:43,144
[Changun] Did you know

684
00:42:44,270 --> 00:42:47,315
the person who hired Cho Pilgu...
[inhales sharply]

685
00:42:50,818 --> 00:42:52,987
...to kill Kim Younghwan was Yu Seongwon?

686
00:42:54,697 --> 00:42:56,823
Are you saying
you gave the order to kill him?

687
00:42:56,824 --> 00:42:57,949
Yes.

688
00:42:57,950 --> 00:42:59,077
Why?

689
00:42:59,952 --> 00:43:02,038
Just because. I thought it'd be fun.

690
00:43:03,706 --> 00:43:04,998
No.

691
00:43:04,999 --> 00:43:08,293
You knew, and that's why you ordered
your secretary, Han Jonghyeon,

692
00:43:08,294 --> 00:43:11,380
to kill Cho Pilgu while he was in custody.
Isn't that right?

693
00:43:12,465 --> 00:43:13,466
I...

694
00:43:15,259 --> 00:43:16,552
didn't know anything.

695
00:43:17,386 --> 00:43:18,429
I'm telling the truth.

696
00:43:28,439 --> 00:43:30,023
Well done.

697
00:43:30,024 --> 00:43:31,734
[Changun] You didn't know anything?

698
00:43:33,569 --> 00:43:37,281
Didn't Detective Joo Hyera
make it clear to you?

699
00:43:39,158 --> 00:43:40,201
Your son is a murderer.

700
00:43:42,370 --> 00:43:43,996
He killed five people.

701
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:47,124
[Taeseon] You know, don't you?

702
00:43:47,125 --> 00:43:48,708
I thought she had it wrong.

703
00:43:48,709 --> 00:43:50,252
I never imagined

704
00:43:50,253 --> 00:43:53,964
that my son could've done
something like that.

705
00:43:53,965 --> 00:43:57,260
Then why did Han Jonghyeon kill Cho Pilgu?

706
00:43:57,969 --> 00:44:00,887
Maybe Seongwon asked him to do it.

707
00:44:00,888 --> 00:44:03,141
They were close, like brothers.

708
00:44:20,449 --> 00:44:21,616
[♪ music fades]

709
00:44:21,617 --> 00:44:24,328
Chairwoman Jeong is still denying
she knows anything.

710
00:44:24,912 --> 00:44:28,249
She claims Yu Seongwon must have
put Han Jonghyeon up to it.

711
00:44:31,127 --> 00:44:32,128
What about Yu Seongwon?

712
00:44:33,462 --> 00:44:35,548
He keeps insisting it wasn't a confession.

713
00:44:36,340 --> 00:44:37,507
[sighs softly]

714
00:44:37,508 --> 00:44:39,260
What about Han Jonghyeon's phone?

715
00:44:39,844 --> 00:44:42,638
There's a record of him calling
the chairwoman, but no recording.

716
00:44:43,222 --> 00:44:44,682
Ah, so... [inhales sharply]

717
00:44:45,349 --> 00:44:48,643
I do have a recording,
but it's from a bug, so we can't use it.

718
00:44:48,644 --> 00:44:49,812
You planted a bug?

719
00:44:50,521 --> 00:44:51,647
Yes.

720
00:44:55,735 --> 00:44:57,277
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

721
00:44:57,278 --> 00:44:58,779
[Taeseon] <i>To cover all this up,</i>

722
00:44:59,655 --> 00:45:01,949
<i>I think Seongwon
will have to commit suicide.</i>

723
00:45:03,201 --> 00:45:05,493
<i>A mentally unstable artist</i>

724
00:45:05,494 --> 00:45:07,496
<i>takes his life
after his studio burns down.</i>

725
00:45:08,247 --> 00:45:10,291
The murder cases are closed unsolved.

726
00:45:15,004 --> 00:45:16,631
And I'll become a poor mother

727
00:45:18,549 --> 00:45:20,801
who lost her child.

728
00:45:22,678 --> 00:45:24,096
[exhales incredulously]

729
00:45:24,805 --> 00:45:26,974
She told him to kill her own son.

730
00:45:28,476 --> 00:45:30,728
That's why Yu Seongwon killed
Han Jonghyeon.

731
00:45:32,355 --> 00:45:35,565
Detective Park and Detective Choi
witnessed that, so we can prove that.

732
00:45:35,566 --> 00:45:36,733
No.

733
00:45:36,734 --> 00:45:39,527
Han Jonghyeon had a gun,

734
00:45:39,528 --> 00:45:41,072
so he'll just claim self-defense.

735
00:45:42,573 --> 00:45:44,783
If we want to prove his serial murders...

736
00:45:44,784 --> 00:45:46,452
We need something from the studio.

737
00:45:48,829 --> 00:45:51,374
We need to unmask that woman, too.

738
00:45:54,085 --> 00:45:56,379
You should talk to the police chief.

739
00:45:57,088 --> 00:45:59,924
I can't go into detail
because I made a promise,

740
00:46:00,591 --> 00:46:02,009
but I think they know each other.

741
00:46:05,429 --> 00:46:06,472
[♪ music fades]

742
00:46:07,723 --> 00:46:08,724
[door opens]

743
00:46:09,684 --> 00:46:11,393
[Taegyun] What?

744
00:46:11,394 --> 00:46:12,520
What is it?

745
00:46:14,730 --> 00:46:17,566
Chairwoman Jeong Taeseon
mentioned you, sir.

746
00:46:19,402 --> 00:46:20,403
How did this happen?

747
00:46:21,862 --> 00:46:24,699
I only told her we had a suspect.

748
00:46:25,324 --> 00:46:27,575
That's all I told her. About Hwang Jongsu.

749
00:46:27,576 --> 00:46:29,995
- How could you tell her that?
- [nervously] Uh...

750
00:46:29,996 --> 00:46:31,997
I really didn't know!

751
00:46:31,998 --> 00:46:36,001
How could I have known
that Yu Seongwon really was a killer?

752
00:46:36,002 --> 00:46:38,670
Chief Park, what do I do?

753
00:46:38,671 --> 00:46:40,463
What do I do?

754
00:46:40,464 --> 00:46:42,340
What am I going to do?

755
00:46:42,341 --> 00:46:43,676
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

756
00:46:55,313 --> 00:46:58,691
What happened with the Hwang Jongsu case?

757
00:46:59,608 --> 00:47:00,735
Hwang Jongsu?

758
00:47:02,445 --> 00:47:04,612
How is that a case? He committed suicide.

759
00:47:04,613 --> 00:47:05,614
[bangs table]

760
00:47:06,198 --> 00:47:07,867
Inducing suicide is a crime, too.

761
00:47:09,952 --> 00:47:11,995
I know the police chief
gave you information

762
00:47:11,996 --> 00:47:13,497
about our suspect, Hwang Jongsu.

763
00:47:14,498 --> 00:47:17,543
Did you send reporters there
to put pressure on Detective Jin,

764
00:47:18,252 --> 00:47:19,669
then tell Hwang to commit suicide?

765
00:47:19,670 --> 00:47:21,297
What are you talking about?

766
00:47:22,923 --> 00:47:26,343
He asked me to send our news team
because detectives were chasing him.

767
00:47:26,344 --> 00:47:30,014
He said he wanted to go on camera
and declare his innocence.

768
00:47:31,640 --> 00:47:33,308
Mr. Hwang probably died

769
00:47:33,309 --> 00:47:35,226
because of Jin Isoo.

770
00:47:35,227 --> 00:47:37,103
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

771
00:47:37,104 --> 00:47:38,564
Maybe he pushed him from behind.

772
00:47:43,069 --> 00:47:44,195
Over here.

773
00:47:46,030 --> 00:47:47,698
[police dogs panting]

774
00:47:49,450 --> 00:47:51,077
[♪ music increases in tempo]

775
00:47:51,744 --> 00:47:52,912
[sniffing eagerly]

776
00:47:56,791 --> 00:47:58,667
[police dogs panting, sniffing]

777
00:48:02,671 --> 00:48:04,590
[barking]

778
00:48:08,260 --> 00:48:10,095
[both barking]

779
00:48:10,096 --> 00:48:12,514
[♪ music swells, fades]

780
00:48:12,515 --> 00:48:16,226
Your mom seems determined
to pin everything on you.

781
00:48:16,227 --> 00:48:18,853
She says you ordered
the murder of Cho Pilgu.

782
00:48:18,854 --> 00:48:20,355
She says she knows nothing.

783
00:48:20,356 --> 00:48:22,023
Who's Cho Pilgu?

784
00:48:22,024 --> 00:48:23,650
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

785
00:48:23,651 --> 00:48:27,571
Can you prove a single thing
you've been saying?

786
00:48:28,781 --> 00:48:30,573
All the people you claim I killed

787
00:48:30,574 --> 00:48:32,492
were still alive after they met me.

788
00:48:32,493 --> 00:48:36,079
The murder display in my studio?

789
00:48:36,080 --> 00:48:37,081
It burned down.

790
00:48:38,040 --> 00:48:39,999
Cho Pilgu, who killed Kim Younghwan,

791
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:41,835
Han Jonghyeon, who killed Cho Pilgu,

792
00:48:41,836 --> 00:48:43,962
and even Mr. Hwang,
the suspect you were chasing,

793
00:48:43,963 --> 00:48:45,338
are all dead.

794
00:48:45,339 --> 00:48:47,215
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

795
00:48:47,216 --> 00:48:48,843
You failed.

796
00:48:50,469 --> 00:48:51,637
Just admit it.

797
00:48:52,638 --> 00:48:54,305
[cell phone vibrating]

798
00:48:54,306 --> 00:48:57,058
DETECTIVE PARK JUNYOUNG

799
00:48:57,059 --> 00:48:58,102
[♪ music swells]

800
00:49:01,439 --> 00:49:02,648
[Junyoung] <i>We found them.</i>

801
00:49:03,482 --> 00:49:06,318
Three bodies were buried in his yard.

802
00:49:13,951 --> 00:49:15,411
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

803
00:49:16,745 --> 00:49:18,289
We found the bodies in your yard.

804
00:49:21,750 --> 00:49:23,627
You buried the bodies in your yard,

805
00:49:24,712 --> 00:49:26,046
walked over them,

806
00:49:27,006 --> 00:49:28,007
and drank tea,

807
00:49:32,678 --> 00:49:34,805
making them look up to you even in death.

808
00:49:36,265 --> 00:49:37,266
You're right.

809
00:49:39,310 --> 00:49:40,686
Because they're mine.

810
00:49:46,650 --> 00:49:48,068
They're mine.

811
00:49:53,699 --> 00:49:55,701
Mine.

812
00:49:56,785 --> 00:50:01,039
Even their bodies rotting inside the earth

813
00:50:01,040 --> 00:50:03,000
are all mine.

814
00:50:03,459 --> 00:50:05,793
- [bangs table]
- [angrily] They're my art!

815
00:50:05,794 --> 00:50:07,546
[shuddering breath of rage]

816
00:50:09,423 --> 00:50:10,633
So this is your ending.

817
00:50:14,512 --> 00:50:17,306
A murderer who pretended to be an artist.

818
00:50:18,098 --> 00:50:19,350
No.

819
00:50:20,184 --> 00:50:23,062
My name, my art

820
00:50:23,687 --> 00:50:25,105
will become even more famous.

821
00:50:26,315 --> 00:50:28,024
[yelling] The whole world

822
00:50:28,025 --> 00:50:30,528
will remember me forever.

823
00:50:31,028 --> 00:50:32,655
[shuddering breath of rage]

824
00:50:35,241 --> 00:50:36,242
You're right.

825
00:50:36,742 --> 00:50:37,993
[in a low voice] Ah...

826
00:50:38,827 --> 00:50:40,538
- [Isoo] That's true.
- [chuckling]

827
00:50:43,707 --> 00:50:44,708
But you

828
00:50:45,584 --> 00:50:46,794
won't get to see that.

829
00:50:47,461 --> 00:50:48,587
You'll be behind bars.

830
00:50:50,130 --> 00:50:51,549
Actually, instead of prison,

831
00:50:52,424 --> 00:50:54,634
you might end up
in a psychiatric hospital.

832
00:50:54,635 --> 00:50:56,595
[♪ melancholy piano music playing]

833
00:51:00,599 --> 00:51:01,600
What a shame.

834
00:51:02,726 --> 00:51:04,770
You hate being locked up
in a hospital room.

835
00:51:06,313 --> 00:51:08,065
Dr. Seo told me everything.

836
00:51:10,401 --> 00:51:12,444
Looks like you'll be wearing
a straitjacket again.

837
00:51:14,530 --> 00:51:15,613
[chuckles softly]

838
00:51:15,614 --> 00:51:16,615
Have fun.

839
00:51:18,826 --> 00:51:20,160
[Seongwon's breath trembling]

840
00:51:23,122 --> 00:51:25,207
[screaming]

841
00:51:28,085 --> 00:51:30,004
[♪ somber, ominous music playing]

842
00:51:31,380 --> 00:51:32,923
[breathing raggedly]

843
00:51:34,091 --> 00:51:35,175
[gasping sharply]

844
00:51:39,096 --> 00:51:41,140
[whimpering brokenly]

845
00:51:46,270 --> 00:51:48,731
[screaming hysterically]

846
00:51:59,491 --> 00:52:00,700
[♪ music fades]

847
00:52:00,701 --> 00:52:02,453
I think I've cooperated enough.

848
00:52:03,537 --> 00:52:05,414
- Need I do more?
- Let's stop here.

849
00:52:18,802 --> 00:52:19,845
[sighs wearily]

850
00:52:22,973 --> 00:52:23,974
Chairwoman.

851
00:52:25,517 --> 00:52:26,518
Where are you going?

852
00:52:29,104 --> 00:52:30,313
Ms. Jeong Taeseon.

853
00:52:30,314 --> 00:52:35,109
You are under arrest for soliciting
the murder of Cho Pilgu and Yu Seongwon.

854
00:52:35,110 --> 00:52:37,154
What are you doing? Do you have proof?

855
00:52:37,905 --> 00:52:41,825
I played this for your son,
and he hit the roof.

856
00:52:43,535 --> 00:52:45,245
[Taeseon] <i>To cover all this up,</i>

857
00:52:46,455 --> 00:52:48,707
<i>I think Seongwon
will have to commit suicide.</i>

858
00:52:49,625 --> 00:52:51,876
<i>A mentally unstable artist</i>

859
00:52:51,877 --> 00:52:53,796
<i>takes his life
after his studio burns down.</i>

860
00:52:55,464 --> 00:52:56,756
[scoffs sarcastically]

861
00:52:56,757 --> 00:52:57,840
[breathes deeply]

862
00:52:57,841 --> 00:52:59,634
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

863
00:52:59,635 --> 00:53:01,177
You bugged my office?

864
00:53:01,178 --> 00:53:02,512
Yes.

865
00:53:02,513 --> 00:53:04,514
See? What did I tell you?

866
00:53:04,515 --> 00:53:07,434
You should've come here
wearing the 18-karat bracelet I gave you.

867
00:53:08,102 --> 00:53:09,394
Just look at the mess you're in.

868
00:53:09,395 --> 00:53:10,562
It breaks my heart.

869
00:53:11,271 --> 00:53:14,357
Go inside and talk to our handsome chief.
Go back inside.

870
00:53:14,358 --> 00:53:15,900
- Jin Isoo.
- Hurry back inside.

871
00:53:15,901 --> 00:53:19,654
Jin Isoo. I'll make you pay for this!

872
00:53:19,655 --> 00:53:21,239
I'll make you pay!

873
00:53:21,240 --> 00:53:22,449
Oh, I'm not scared at all.

874
00:53:23,033 --> 00:53:24,201
[chuckles]

875
00:53:25,327 --> 00:53:26,495
[door closes]

876
00:53:28,288 --> 00:53:29,372
SHOCKING ARREST OF MOTHER AND SON

877
00:53:29,373 --> 00:53:30,790
A CONFESSION THAT SHOCKED THE WORLD

878
00:53:30,791 --> 00:53:32,041
[camera shutter clicking]

879
00:53:32,042 --> 00:53:33,418
POLICE CHIEF FACES DISCIPLINARY HEARING

880
00:53:33,419 --> 00:53:35,294
MOTHER SOLICITS MURDER TO PROTECT HER SON

881
00:53:35,295 --> 00:53:36,838
JIN ISOO HOLDS JOINT FUNERAL FOR VICTIMS

882
00:53:36,839 --> 00:53:38,881
MAY THEY REST IN PEACE

883
00:53:38,882 --> 00:53:41,050
HANSU GROUP,
GANGHA POLICE STATION, JOO HYERA

884
00:53:41,051 --> 00:53:43,469
OUR DEEPEST CONDOLENCES
MAY THEY REST IN PEACE

885
00:53:43,470 --> 00:53:45,972
CHOI YEONGMIN, KIM HEEJUN, JO NAYEONG

886
00:53:45,973 --> 00:53:48,015
[♪ somber, melancholy music playing]

887
00:53:48,016 --> 00:53:49,476
Let us have a moment of silence.

888
00:53:50,686 --> 00:53:52,103
[woman sobbing]

889
00:53:52,104 --> 00:53:53,564
[scattered sobbing]

890
00:53:58,402 --> 00:53:59,403
Thank you.

891
00:54:01,155 --> 00:54:03,115
[scattered sobbing, sniffling]

892
00:54:07,828 --> 00:54:09,163
[woman sobbing bitterly]

893
00:54:11,582 --> 00:54:13,499
[scattered sobbing, sniffling continues]

894
00:54:13,500 --> 00:54:16,085
[woman] I can't bear
to let you go like this.

895
00:54:16,086 --> 00:54:17,755
How can I let you go?

896
00:54:23,469 --> 00:54:25,137
[woman continues sobbing bitterly]

897
00:54:36,440 --> 00:54:37,816
Thank you.

898
00:54:47,701 --> 00:54:49,119
[breath trembles, sniffles]

899
00:55:04,051 --> 00:55:06,261
[♪ somber, melancholy music continues]

900
00:55:35,624 --> 00:55:36,667
[♪ music fades]

901
00:55:39,419 --> 00:55:42,630
I suddenly couldn't breathe
and my body just froze.

902
00:55:42,631 --> 00:55:44,674
I couldn't even trust myself.

903
00:55:44,675 --> 00:55:48,136
I even wondered
if I should quit being a cop.

904
00:55:49,388 --> 00:55:50,973
But after I caught Yu Seongwon,

905
00:55:51,640 --> 00:55:54,893
I've been sleeping well,
and I feel more at ease.

906
00:55:56,019 --> 00:55:58,479
I somehow feel like
I can get through this.

907
00:55:58,480 --> 00:55:59,481
I'm glad to hear that.

908
00:56:00,190 --> 00:56:02,900
I think doing meaningful work
is helping you get better.

909
00:56:02,901 --> 00:56:04,360
Exactly.

910
00:56:04,361 --> 00:56:07,030
Thank goodness I became a detective.

911
00:56:07,906 --> 00:56:11,410
Investigating is so much fun,
catching bad guys is so rewarding,

912
00:56:11,785 --> 00:56:13,787
and my teammates... [chuckles softly]

913
00:56:14,288 --> 00:56:16,748
They're clueless, but they're good people.

914
00:56:17,666 --> 00:56:19,750
Would you like to see? Here.

915
00:56:19,751 --> 00:56:20,918
[♪ jaunty music playing]

916
00:56:20,919 --> 00:56:23,462
This tall, feeble-looking one
is Detective Joo.

917
00:56:23,463 --> 00:56:24,589
- Okay.
- The right, tall one.

918
00:56:24,590 --> 00:56:26,382
He has a girlfriend now. He's Junyoung.

919
00:56:26,383 --> 00:56:28,426
The curly hair is our youngest teammate.

920
00:56:28,427 --> 00:56:30,344
He claims he has a girlfriend.

921
00:56:30,345 --> 00:56:32,013
And this good-looking man here.

922
00:56:32,014 --> 00:56:34,390
That's me. This is
Violent Crime Investigation Team 1.

923
00:56:34,391 --> 00:56:35,892
- I see.
- Amazing, right?

924
00:56:36,643 --> 00:56:38,019
Gangha Police Violent Crime Team 1,

925
00:56:38,020 --> 00:56:39,895
in investigating a serial murder case

926
00:56:39,896 --> 00:56:43,232
whose perpetrator had long evaded
capture through sophisticated methods,

927
00:56:43,233 --> 00:56:47,194
apprehended the suspect with outstanding
investigative skill and determination,

928
00:56:47,195 --> 00:56:50,781
and demonstrated exemplary dedication
and devotion to duty as police officers,

929
00:56:50,782 --> 00:56:52,491
and is hereby commended.

930
00:56:52,492 --> 00:56:56,120
Gangha Police Violent Crime Team 1,
Senior Inspector Joo Hyera.

931
00:56:56,121 --> 00:56:57,331
[all applauding]

932
00:56:59,583 --> 00:57:00,666
What's wrong with you?

933
00:57:00,667 --> 00:57:03,836
[announcer] Gangha Police Violent Crime
Team 1, Senior Inspector Jin Isoo.

934
00:57:03,837 --> 00:57:05,547
[all applauding]

935
00:57:10,260 --> 00:57:11,344
[loudly] Thank you, sir!

936
00:57:11,345 --> 00:57:12,887
[laughing]

937
00:57:12,888 --> 00:57:14,889
[announcer] Inspector Park Junyoung.

938
00:57:14,890 --> 00:57:17,558
[squeals] You're so handsome,
Park Junyoung!

939
00:57:17,559 --> 00:57:19,061
[all applauding]

940
00:57:19,811 --> 00:57:20,896
[loudly] Thank you, sir!

941
00:57:22,314 --> 00:57:24,065
[announcer] Senior Police Officer
Choi Kyungjin.

942
00:57:24,066 --> 00:57:25,441
[all applauding]

943
00:57:25,442 --> 00:57:26,443
[loudly] Thank you, sir!

944
00:57:27,194 --> 00:57:29,153
Hurry up and get in here. Ready?

945
00:57:29,154 --> 00:57:31,113
- One, two, three!
- [camera shutter clicks]

946
00:57:31,114 --> 00:57:32,115
Perfect.

947
00:57:33,450 --> 00:57:34,533
Huh?

948
00:57:34,534 --> 00:57:37,496
Mr. Choi, I think
you're late for your flight.

949
00:57:38,038 --> 00:57:39,039
I'm not late.

950
00:57:39,623 --> 00:57:41,540
Ah! You're late. Let's take my car.

951
00:57:41,541 --> 00:57:43,167
- [Mr. Choi] I'm fine.
- Let's go. We're off.

952
00:57:43,168 --> 00:57:45,003
- Sorry, goodbye.
- No problem. Goodbye.

953
00:57:45,671 --> 00:57:46,754
[♪ music fades]

954
00:57:46,755 --> 00:57:48,006
[engine purring smoothly]

955
00:57:55,055 --> 00:57:57,224
Are you really going to go like that?

956
00:57:58,642 --> 00:58:01,686
Why would you wear
a suit on a trip to Europe?

957
00:58:01,687 --> 00:58:03,604
I told you, I'm comfortable in this.

958
00:58:03,605 --> 00:58:05,857
But it's a long-haul flight.

959
00:58:07,192 --> 00:58:09,777
- [sighs in exasperation] I give up.
- [chuckles]

960
00:58:09,778 --> 00:58:11,237
[♪ gentle, tender music playing]

961
00:58:11,238 --> 00:58:14,366
Have fun, get plenty of rest,
and take your full vacation.

962
00:58:14,950 --> 00:58:17,077
All right. Thank you.

963
00:58:18,078 --> 00:58:19,412
Did you pack your meds?

964
00:58:19,413 --> 00:58:20,871
If anything happens--

965
00:58:20,872 --> 00:58:23,165
Ah, all right, now stop.

966
00:58:23,166 --> 00:58:26,627
[sighs] I'm worried.
Maybe I should go with you.

967
00:58:26,628 --> 00:58:29,088
I heard your team is
going on vacation as a reward.

968
00:58:29,089 --> 00:58:30,965
We can change the destination to Europe.

969
00:58:30,966 --> 00:58:32,551
I must decline.

970
00:58:33,760 --> 00:58:34,928
[chuckles softly]

971
00:58:38,348 --> 00:58:39,516
[both chuckle]

972
00:58:40,308 --> 00:58:41,351
[♪ music fades]

973
00:58:46,523 --> 00:58:47,941
Have a great trip.

974
00:58:48,900 --> 00:58:50,652
All right. Take care.

975
00:58:51,570 --> 00:58:54,156
I don't feel good sending you off so far.

976
00:58:55,115 --> 00:58:56,116
How about a hug?

977
00:58:56,700 --> 00:58:57,783
[chuckles]

978
00:58:57,784 --> 00:58:59,285
[♪ gentle, tender music playing]

979
00:58:59,286 --> 00:59:00,287
[chuckles softly]

980
00:59:00,662 --> 00:59:01,830
[Isoo exhales contentedly]

981
00:59:02,998 --> 00:59:03,999
Mmm.

982
00:59:09,921 --> 00:59:10,922
I'll be back soon.

983
00:59:12,132 --> 00:59:13,215
Go on inside.

984
00:59:13,216 --> 00:59:14,217
[chuckles softly]

985
00:59:23,977 --> 00:59:24,978
[sighs contentedly]

986
00:59:29,691 --> 00:59:30,776
Mr. Choi Jeonghun.

987
00:59:31,943 --> 00:59:33,903
Oh! [chortles]

988
00:59:33,904 --> 00:59:35,362
Hello.

989
00:59:35,363 --> 00:59:37,323
Where are you going? A business trip?

990
00:59:37,324 --> 00:59:38,366
No.

991
00:59:39,201 --> 00:59:40,367
I'm going on vacation.

992
00:59:40,368 --> 00:59:41,494
Finally.

993
00:59:41,495 --> 00:59:43,621
- Wow.
- [both chuckle]

994
00:59:43,622 --> 00:59:44,998
I'm leaving today, too.

995
00:59:45,624 --> 00:59:47,209
- Really?
- Where are you headed?

996
00:59:48,043 --> 00:59:49,376
I'm going to...

997
00:59:49,377 --> 00:59:50,629
[♪ music increases in tempo]

998
01:00:00,263 --> 01:00:01,264
Me too.

999
01:00:03,725 --> 01:00:04,934
[chuckles]

1000
01:00:04,935 --> 01:00:06,102
[chuckles softly]

1001
01:00:08,939 --> 01:00:10,147
[♪ music fades]

1002
01:00:10,148 --> 01:00:11,900
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

1003
01:00:15,946 --> 01:00:17,113
[exhales contentedly]

1004
01:00:22,202 --> 01:00:24,912
Bro. I thought we were going abroad.

1005
01:00:24,913 --> 01:00:26,705
We can't just take off as Korean cops.

1006
01:00:26,706 --> 01:00:28,666
We have a country to protect.

1007
01:00:28,667 --> 01:00:29,918
Having said that,

1008
01:00:30,627 --> 01:00:32,337
this is our reward vacation.

1009
01:00:32,963 --> 01:00:34,755
Yeah. [exhales contentedly]

1010
01:00:34,756 --> 01:00:38,008
I can't remember the last time
I had a break like this.

1011
01:00:38,009 --> 01:00:39,219
[sighs contentedly]

1012
01:00:40,220 --> 01:00:41,303
What's taking so long?

1013
01:00:41,304 --> 01:00:43,472
Women always take forever.

1014
01:00:43,473 --> 01:00:46,601
Oh. What are they even doing in there?
[scoffs]

1015
01:00:59,614 --> 01:01:00,739
Are you going for a dive?

1016
01:01:00,740 --> 01:01:02,116
Whatever.

1017
01:01:02,117 --> 01:01:04,870
- Is this good?
- What's with the whistle?

1018
01:01:05,829 --> 01:01:06,997
Aren't we going out there?

1019
01:01:09,791 --> 01:01:11,418
Right, we should.

1020
01:01:12,085 --> 01:01:13,794
- Let's go!
- Move out!

1021
01:01:13,795 --> 01:01:14,963
- [Kyungjin] Let's go!
- [Isoo] Let's go!

1022
01:01:17,757 --> 01:01:19,049
REWARD VACATION!!
JIN ISOO'S TREAT!

1023
01:01:19,050 --> 01:01:20,634
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

1024
01:01:20,635 --> 01:01:22,053
- Whoo!
- [screaming]

1025
01:02:11,519 --> 01:02:12,604
[♪ music fades]

1026
01:02:15,482 --> 01:02:17,442
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

1027
01:02:41,716 --> 01:02:43,301
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1028
01:02:45,470 --> 01:02:46,638
[♪ music swells]

1029
01:03:06,366 --> 01:03:07,617
[exhales heavily]

1030
01:03:13,623 --> 01:03:14,708
[♪ music fades]

1031
01:03:19,713 --> 01:03:20,796
[exhales softly]

1032
01:03:20,797 --> 01:03:22,716
Jin Isoo, get changed.

1033
01:03:23,425 --> 01:03:24,426
Why?

1034
01:03:24,968 --> 01:03:26,094
[sighs] We have a case.

1035
01:03:27,887 --> 01:03:28,888
A case?

1036
01:03:30,932 --> 01:03:32,266
Looks like we've got ourselves...

1037
01:03:32,267 --> 01:03:34,019
A most interesting case, right?

1038
01:03:36,771 --> 01:03:38,313
Let's go, Detective Joo.

1039
01:03:38,314 --> 01:03:40,066
[microphone feedback]

1040
01:03:42,068 --> 01:03:43,069
We have a case.

1041
01:03:43,737 --> 01:03:44,820
Let's go.

1042
01:03:44,821 --> 01:03:47,032
[♪ theme music playing]

1043
01:04:17,395 --> 01:04:18,479
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 14

1044
01:04:18,480 --> 01:04:19,856
VIOLENT CRIME TEAM 1
OFF TO THE NEXT CASE!

1045
01:04:40,960 --> 01:04:44,463
Special Cast. Yoo Seungho

1046
01:04:44,464 --> 01:04:47,966
Special Cast. Kim Hyeeun

1047
01:04:47,967 --> 01:04:51,387
Special Cast. Kim Jihun

1048
01:04:58,186 --> 01:04:59,979
JIN ISOO
AHN BOHYUN

1049
01:05:03,191 --> 01:05:04,984
JOO HYERA
JUNG EUNCHAE

1050
01:05:07,070 --> 01:05:08,988
PARK JUNYOUNG
KANG SANGJUN

1051
01:05:11,116 --> 01:05:12,992
CHOI KYUNGJIN
KIM SHINBI

1052
01:05:15,120 --> 01:05:16,955
YOON JIWON
JUNG GAHEE

1053
01:05:20,291 --> 01:05:22,126
YU SEONGWON
YOO SEUNGHO

1054
01:05:22,127 --> 01:05:24,169
